      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "After intravenous administration of aniracetam to rats, the metabolite 2-pyrrolidinone distributed into brain regions with an AUCbrain/AUCplasma ratio of 53-55%.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple high-transfer direct in-vivo records demonstrate BBB/CSF penetration after systemic administration across rats, mice, humans, baboons, rabbits, and guinea-pigs. The only mixed record is species-dependent and does not overturn the consistent positive evidence, so meaningful CNS access is supported.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "One retrieved molecule showed species-dependent brain detection (absent in rat brain, present in guinea-pig brain), adding minor uncertainty.",
    "Quantitative human CNS exposure is mostly derived from CSF measurements in tuberculous meningitis; healthy human quantitative data are not provided."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
